Z||000023||sloth85GT||08-13-2001||06:12 PM||||I just went down to Toysport and we mounted one wheel onto my car with the correct lugs and I noticed that in the back I have VERY little clearance on my strut. But the key idea here is that I DO still have clearance. So it'll all be good. But now I have to wait ANOTHER 2 weeks until the lugs come in. It won't be so bad seeing as how I'm in Vancouver and Calgary from the 19th till the 28th. So they should be here when I get back. <P>I also noticed one bad thing.......I mentioned in another thread that I had a clunking sound coming from the right rear of my car when I make left turns. Well........when I had the car up, I realized that the wheel wobbles. Not a great deal, but it does. Could that be the bearings? What else could be the problem?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif"> <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
